# === Frozen POC ===
#
# This is the most fragile defense of the three POC files: unlike lint, which
# only complains, `pnpm format` WRITES. Without these three lines, the first
# `pnpm format` silently reformats the POC that is published and live until
# the Phase 6 cutover.
#
# FR-016 and SC-006 of spec 001. Do not remove without reading.
index.html
script.js
style.css

# === Generated ===
dist/
.astro/
node_modules/
coverage/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# === Maintained by the Spec Kit CLI ===
#
# .specify/ and .claude/skills/speckit-* are generated and maintained by the
# CLI, pinned at 1.2.5. The constitution requires that updating the CLI be an
# explicit decision "with the init diff reviewed" -- reformatting here makes
# that diff unreadable. Applies to YAML and JSON, not just markdown.
.specify/
.claude/

# === Markdown ===
#
# Prettier formats CODE in this repository, not prose. The reason was found in
# practice, not by taste: running `pnpm format` without this rule rewrote 15
# documentation files at once, in two harmful ways.
#
# 1. It rewrote .claude/skills/speckit-*/SKILL.md -- including the quoting of
#    the YAML frontmatter. Those files are maintained by the Spec Kit CLI,
#    pinned at 1.2.5, and the constitution requires being able to review the
#    `init` diff when updating. Reformatting them makes that diff unreadable
#    and touches the definition of the skills that make the process exist.
#
# 2. It stretched the tables in AGENTS.md beyond 100 columns. The documentation
#    in this repo is hand-written at ~80 columns because it is read in a
#    terminal, by people and by agents. Prettier's table padding works against
#    that.
#
# What is lost: markdown is not covered by `pnpm format:check`. Accepted --
# line wrapping in prose is the writer's decision, not a tool's.
*.md
